{"id":51,"name":"dugtrio","speciesId":51,"dex":51,"form":"normal","generation":1,"types":["ground"],"stats":{"hp":35,"attack":100,"defense":50,"special-attack":50,"special-defense":70,"speed":120},"abilities":[{"name":"sand-veil","hidden":false},{"name":"arena-trap","hidden":false},{"name":"sand-force","hidden":true}],"height":7,"weight":333,"baseExp":149,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/51.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/51.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/51.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/51.ogg","genus":"Mole Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"red","text":"A team of DIGLETT triplets. It triggers huge earthquakes by burrowing 60 miles underground."},{"version":"yellow","text":"A team of triplets that can burrow over 60 MPH. Due to this, some people think it's an earthquake."},{"version":"gold","text":"Its three heads bob separately up and down to loosen the soil nearby, making it easier for it to burrow."},{"version":"silver","text":"Extremely power­ ful, they can DIG through even the hardest ground to a depth of over 60 miles."},{"version":"crystal","text":"These DIGLETT triplets dig over 60 miles below sea level. No one knows what it's like underground."},{"version":"ruby","text":"DUGTRIO are actually triplets that emerged from one body. As a result, each triplet thinks exactly like the other two triplets. They work cooperatively to burrow endlessly."},{"version":"emerald","text":"Because the triplets originally split from one body, they think exactly alike. They work cooperatively to burrow endlessly through the ground."},{"version":"firered","text":"In battle, it digs through the ground and strikes the unsuspecting foe from an unexpected direction."},{"version":"diamond","text":"Its three heads move alternately, driving it through tough soil to depths of over 60 miles."},{"version":"soulsilver","text":"Extremely powerful, they can dig through even the hardest ground to a depth of over 60 miles."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"Dugtrio are actually triplets that emerged from one body. As a result, each triplet thinks exactly like the other two triplets. They work cooperatively to burrow endlessly."},{"version":"sun","text":"This set of triplets moves cooperatively. It’s the power of teamwork that enables this Pokémon to dig to a depth of 60 miles."},{"version":"moon","text":"Despite the closeness between this Pokémon and farmers and other people, no one has ever seen the parts of it concealed underground."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"While the three of them normally get along splendidly, on rare occasions a huge fight will break out over which head gets to eat first."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"Dugtrio’s heads are sleek and smooth and incredibly hard. It can dig through any soil with its headbutts."},{"version":"lets-go-pikachu","text":"A team of triplets that can burrow to a depth of 60 miles. It’s reported that this triggers an earthquake."},{"version":"sword","text":"A team of Diglett triplets. It triggers huge earthquakes by burrowing 60 miles underground."},{"version":"shield","text":"These Diglett triplets dig over 60 miles below sea level. No one knows what it’s like underground."}],"genderRate":4,"captureRate":50,"eggGroups":["ground"],"isLegendary":false,"isMythical":false,"evolution":{"species":"diglett","speciesId":50,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions":["Nível 26","Nível 26"],"species":"dugtrio","speciesId":51,"evolvesTo":[]}]},"varieties":[{"id":51,"name":"dugtrio","form":"normal","sprite":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/51.png"},{"id":10106,"name":"dugtrio-alola","form":"alolan","sprite":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official